ADDENDA <Act No. 16433, Apr. 30, 2019>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 1 year after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to labeling on containers)
Articles 13 through 15 shall begin to apply to in vitro diagnostic medical devices taken out from a factory or bonded area on or after the date this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning permission, certification, and notification)
(1) A person who has obtained manufacturing business permission or import business permission under the Medical Devices Act as at the time this Act enters into force and manufactures or imports in vitro diagnostic medical devices shall be deemed to have obtained permission under Article 5 (1) or 11 (1); provided, he or she shall have facilities and manufacturing and quality management systems under the main clause of Article 5 (5) or the main clause of Article 11 (4) within 2 years after this Act enters into force.
(2) If an in vitro diagnostic medical device has obtained manufacturing permission, manufacturing certification, import permission, or import certification, or has filed a manufacturing notification or an import notification under the Medical Devices Act, as at the time this Act enters into force, it shall be deemed to have obtained such permission or certification, or to have filed such notification under Article 5 (3) or 11 (2).
Article 4 (Transitional Measures concerning Clinical Performance Study Institutions)
An institution designated as a clinical performance study institution under Article 10 (3) of the Medical Devices Act as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed designated as a clinical performance study institution under Article 8 (1); provided, it shall file an application for designation as a clinical performance study institution under this Act within 1 year after this Act enters into force and shall re-obtain such designation within one year after this Act enters into force.
Article 5 (Transitional Measures concerning Matters to Be Stated in Containers)
Notwithstanding Articles 13 through 15, containers, packages, or accompanying documents stating matters to be entered under Articles 20 through 22 of the Medical Devices Act as at the time this Act enters into force may be used for 2 years from the date this Act enters into force.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning dispositions)
Public notice, disposition, and other acts related to in vitro diagnostic medical devices and applications, reports, and other acts filed with or done to administrative agencies under the Medical Devices Act before this Act enters into force shall be deemed acts done by or done to administrative agencies under this Act corresponding thereto.
Article 7 (Transitional Measures concerning Administrative Dispositions)
The Medical Devices Act shall apply to administrative dispositions taken against violations of the Medical Devices Act before this Act enters into force.
Article 8 (Transitional Measures concerning Penalty Provisions)
The Medical Devices Act shall apply to the application of penalty provisions to any violation of the Medical Devices Act before this Act enters into force.
Article 9 (Relationship to Other Statutes and Regulations)
Where the Medical Devices Act or any provision thereof is cited by other statutes or regulations as at the time this Act enters into force, if any provision corresponding thereto exists in this Act, this Act or the corresponding provision of this Act shall be deemed cited together.

